# Downloaded toolchain. Pinned versions are recorded in
# docs/research/document-remediation/experiment-plan.md; fetch-tools.sh
# reproduces this directory. ~50MB of JARs does not belong in git.
vendor/

# Every generated artefact: corpus PDFs and raw validator output. Regenerable
# from corpus/ sources. Summarised numbers that survive are committed under
# docs/research/document-remediation/.
out/

# Real client-like documents pulled from public municipal sites, and the ground
# truth hand-authored for them. Both stay local: the source files are somebody
# else's bytes, and ground truth quotes their text. Nothing here is regenerable
# from the repo, so it is listed in real/SOURCES.md instead — URLs and hashes,
# not content.
real/
# Arm A corpus: generated bytes stay out, authored keys stay in.
word-corpus/*
!word-corpus/keys
real-word/
out-arm-a/
real-word-truth/
out-arm-a-real/
# The rule that just failed: EVERY real-bytes directory is named here BEFORE
# its first fetch. real-pdf/ was not, and `git add -A` on a results branch
# swept 23 real municipal PDFs onto public master (removed in the same PR as
# this line; history purge is a separate, user-authorized operation).
real-pdf/
out-arm-b-evidence/
